        "original_id": "94b960b2-d0b9-5be7-8f02-04f4cdac0eb2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Pollack, Phil Hill, Philip Toll Hill Jr., Mario Andretti\n- Topics: Post-World War II California sports car culture, Formula One World Drivers' Championship\n\nFacts:\n- Bill Pollack was a competitor in the early days of post-World War II California sports car culture.\n- Bill Pollack was a contemporary of Phil Hill.\n- Philip Toll Hill Jr. was born on April 20, 1927, and died on August 28, 2008.\n- Phil Hill was an American automobile racer.\n- Phil Hill was the first and only American-born driver to win the Formula One World Drivers' Championship.\n- Mario Andretti won the World Drivers' Championship in 1978, but he was not born in the United States.",
